    "selector": 3,
    "compatibility": "V1 remains exactly strict false-visibility; V2 remains exactly the reviewed pure conjunct shape. Neither silently accepts structure exclusions.",
    "allowlist": "Only the eight exact code.lua IDs/source hashes/spans below. New sources, shapes or widened spans require another independent schema/feature decision.",
    "visibility": "module_observable must be true. Public binary output makes private optimizer choices observable; this says nothing about a public promise of exact C optimization.",
    "compatibility_obligation": "module_compatibility_obligation, public_api and mixed_obligation must all be false after independent feature and retained-semantic review.",
    "source_only": "Installed exclusion children must have empty evidence and never status passed. Lexical references and actual runtime obligations remain distinct.",
    "original_anchors": "Preserve all51 original records and their exact identities. Derive8 new private children. Eighteen contained lexical anchors need independent reference/decomposition decisions; no implicit status rewrite or parent completion.",
    "protected_history": "Existing protected-scope descriptors, all13 accepted partitions, any previous pass/evidence and public/mixed obligations remain unconditionally ineligible.",
    "two_reviews": "The accepted-feature-only-with-required-revisions artifact is a relevance input, never enough to install exclusions. New independent retention and exact decisions must bind current witness contracts and original-parent decomposition.",
    "transform": "Reuse exact source/policy-bound transforms; empty/complete-comment/punctuation replacements only. No executable replacement, fake T facade, helper short circuit, T=nil or broad flags/returns.",
    "runtime": "Whole original-C/derived-Ada source execution, public counterparts, fresh named receipts, allocator cleanup and final-context envelopes remain separately required.",
    "target_selector": "Available only through explicit TargetPolicy remaining-upstream-compatibility. Existing strict default completion, historical scopes and their semantics remain unchanged."
  },
